{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/behavior/aggregation_validator.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/behavior/aggregation_validator.py around lines 174 - 193, Update _get_source_fields to extract each field descriptor’s name when fields_node contains dictionaries, while retaining string entries as field names. Ensure the resulting set contains actual schema field names such as “x”, so validate_aggregation_config does not report false CMP_PF_AGG_002 missing-field errors.","suggestions":["    def _get_source_fields(self, source_schema: JsonDict) -> set[str]:\n        properties = source_schema.get(\"properties\")\n        if isinstance(properties, dict):\n            return set(properties.keys())\n        fields_node = source_schema.get(\"fields\")\n        if isinstance(fields_node, list):\n            return {\n                str(field[\"name\"])\n                if isinstance(field, dict) and \"name\" in field\n                else str(field)\n                for field in fields_node\n            }\n        return self._collect_fallback_fields(source_schema)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _collect_fallback_fields(source_schema: JsonDict) -> set[str]:\n        \"\"\"Collect field names from explicit schema shapes only.\"\"\"\n        fields: set[str] = set()\n        columns = source_schema.get(\"columns\")\n        if isinstance(columns, list):\n            fields.update(str(item) for item in columns)\n        names = source_schema.get(\"field_names\")\n        if isinstance(names, list):\n            fields.update(str(item) for item in names)\n        return fields"]}
