{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/behavior/schema_classifier_helpers.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/behavior/schema_classifier_helpers.py around lines 34 - 49, Update build_field_type_change to validate old_field and new_field are mappings before calling .get(\"type\"), treating boolean or other non-mapping property values as having no type (or otherwise returning no type-change). Preserve normal comparison and SchemaChange construction for mapping values, and ensure malformed property definitions do not raise AttributeError during SchemaClassifier._calculate_diff.","suggestions":["def build_field_type_change(\n    field_name: str,\n    old_field: object,\n    new_field: object,\n) -> SchemaChange | None:\n    \"\"\"Build type-change schema change when field type changed.\"\"\"\n    old_type = old_field.get(\"type\") if isinstance(old_field, dict) else None\n    new_type = new_field.get(\"type\") if isinstance(new_field, dict) else None\n    if old_type == new_type:\n        return None\n    return SchemaChange(\n        change_type=SchemaChangeType.FIELD_TYPE_CHANGED,\n        field_path=f\"properties.{field_name}.type\",\n        old_value=old_type,\n        new_value=new_type,\n    )"]}
