{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/behavior/text_similarity.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/behavior/text_similarity.py around lines 21 - 36, Update normalize_text to replace all Unicode punctuation characters, including typographic apostrophes, quotation marks, en/em dashes, and non-breaking hyphens, rather than relying only on string.punctuation; preserve whitespace collapsing and case normalization, and add unit tests covering curly apostrophes and em dashes that verify equivalent normalized text and similarity behavior.","suggestions":["from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport string\nimport unicodedata\n\n\ndef normalize_text(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Normalize text for comparison.\n\n    Lowercases, replaces punctuation with spaces, collapses whitespace.\n\n    Args:\n        text: Raw text string.\n\n    Returns:\n        Normalized text. Empty string if input is empty/None-like.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return \"\"\n    normalized = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKC\", text)\n    cleaned = \"\".join(\n        \" \" if (ch in string.punctuation or unicodedata.category(ch).startswith(\"P\"))\n        else ch\n        for ch in normalized\n    )\n    return \" \".join(cleaned.lower().split())"]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/behavior/organism_classification_service_filtering.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/behavior/organism_classification_service_filtering.py around lines 52 - 76, Update build_filter_strategy to reject configurations where both include and exclude are provided, before selecting _include_strategy or _exclude_strategy. Raise the established validation exception with a clear message, while preserving the existing precedence and behavior when only one or neither filter is supplied.","suggestions":["def build_filter_strategy(\n    *,\n    include: set[CellularityType] | None,\n    exclude: set[CellularityType] | None,\n    keep_unresolved: bool,\n) -> CellularityFilterStrategy:\n    \"\"\"Build filter strategy for include/exclude/unresolved policy.\n\n    Precedence: include > exclude > pass-all.\n\n    Args:\n        include: If provided, only records with cellularity in this set are kept.\n        exclude: If provided, records with cellularity in this set are removed.\n        keep_unresolved: Whether records with unknown cellularity are retained.\n\n    Returns:\n        Callable CellularityFilterStrategy that accepts a CellularityType or None\n        and returns True if the record should be kept.\n    \"\"\"\n    # include uses is not None so empty include is explicit filter-none.\n    if include is not None and exclude is not None:\n        raise ValueError(\"include and exclude are mutually exclusive\")\n    if include is not None:\n        return _include_strategy(include, keep_unresolved)\n    if exclude is not None:\n        return _exclude_strategy(exclude, keep_unresolved)\n    return _pass_all_strategy(keep_unresolved)"]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"critical","fileName":"src/bioetl/domain/behavior/staged_enforcement.py","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/bioetl/domain/behavior/staged_enforcement.py around lines 48 - 65, Correct the default threshold values in EnforcementPolicy so warning_threshold is below failure_threshold and a zero failure rate resolves to OBSERVE; preserve the existing stage-selection order. Add validation enforcing failure_threshold > warning_threshold when constructing a policy, and add a unit test covering the default policy’s zero-rate OBSERVE result.","suggestions":["@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass EnforcementPolicy:\n    \"\"\"Policy for staged enforcement.\"\"\"\n\n    check_name: str\n    current_stage: EnforcementStage\n    failure_threshold: float = 1.0\n    warning_threshold: float = 0.5\n    observe_until: str | None = None  # \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n    soft_fail_until: str | None = None  # \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n\n    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reject out-of-range or inverted thresholds.\"\"\"\n        for name in (\"failure_threshold\", \"warning_threshold\"):\n            value = getattr(self, name)\n            if not 0.0 <= value <= 1.0:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be in [0.0, 1.0]\")\n        if self.warning_threshold > self.failure_threshold:\n            raise ValueError(\n                \"warning_threshold must not exceed failure_threshold\"\n            )\n\n    def get_effective_stage(self, failure_rate: float) -> EnforcementStage:\n        \"\"\"Resolve the effective enforcement stage for the observed failure rate.\"\"\"\n        if failure_rate >= self.failure_threshold:\n            return EnforcementStage.HARD_FAIL\n        if failure_rate >= self.warning_threshold:\n            return EnforcementStage.SOFT_FAIL\n        return EnforcementStage.OBSERVE"]}
